WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.410
<i>"Period." The name given to the ones who 
defeat bizarre monsters called "spirals,"</i>

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:10.490
<i>and put an end to the sorrowful cycle.</i>

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.560
<i>We fight for peace,</i>

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.360
<i>and for hope for a better tomorrow.</i>

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.690
<i>Here in the fortress city of Hopeless,</i>

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:25.790
<i>the periods of Arc End Branch #8 
battle the spirals night and day</i>

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.380
<i>along with their young Commander Erika.</i>

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.130
Ice Edge!

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:42.890
Go, Haru!

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.610
<i>I'm going to become a great period here,</i>

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.020
<i>and fulfill my promise!</i>

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.710
<i>We are periods.</i>

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.500
<i>The one hope that can end 
the cycle of despair.</i>

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:04.670
<i>But...</i>

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.900
<b>~ the journey to the end of the despair ~</b>

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.090
<b>Episode 1: Notice of Completion</b>

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.180
It feels like been a long time 
since we've been in Hopeless!

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.390
It's only been two days.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.210
It was fun camping with the four of us!

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.840
Well, it felt a lot more like city 
living than life in the Animal Realm!

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.480
Compared to your homeland,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.000
even the deepest jungle is 
like living in the city!

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.660
Yeah? Aw, I'm blushing.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:03.280
That's not a complement!

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.420
Ow!

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.080
What was that for, Choco?

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.770
I'm hungry.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.140
Stop it, Choco! You're giving me bite marks!

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.190
It'll sting when I take a bath!

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:15.800
We're almost to the Branch Office, okay?

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.560
Huh? It's locked.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.010
What, was the office closed today?

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.710
I didn't hear anything about that.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.580
Maybe there was emergency maintenance?

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.450
If so, we'd better get some free gacha.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:27.740
Choco, did you say something?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.270
There's something on the ground.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.050
What's that? A map?

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.150
It's got something marked on it.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.530
Looks like this is the place.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.900
It's gotta be!

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.830
Looks dumpy.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:45.370
What's in here, anyway?

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.330
We'll know when we go inside!

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.340
Haru-kun!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.470
It's me, your beloved Campanella-san!

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:06.100
I'm so glad... I'm so glad you're back!

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.900
Well, my vacation's over, 
so of course I came back.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.760
What happened?

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.690
Why is the Branch Office closed?

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:19.570
You see, the Arc End Branch 
Office #8 that we loved...

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.650
...is now dead!

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.920
I'll tell you the details inside.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.830
Erika-san is waiting.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.250
Okay.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:35.120
What? The Branch Office's 
treasury was stolen?

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:36.290
Yes.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:43.470
All the zel was stolen from our carefully
guarded treasury before morning two days ago.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:46.640
It was so sudden that we 
couldn't pay any of our bills,

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.100
and we had to sell all the land and 
buildings the Branch Office owned.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:56.150
Branch Office #8 was ordered to shut down.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.140
Who stole it?

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.480
Have we caught them yet?

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.630
There aren't any clues at all.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:06.140
I suggested we do a thorough 
investigation, but...

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:06.950
No.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.490
That would mean suspecting our comrades.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.700
I will always believe in my comrades!

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.020
That's so wonderful, Erika-san!

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:19.100
But saying that means you're convinced 
one of your comrades did it.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.480
You're not supposed to <i>say</i> that, Gajeru.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.270
Um, where are the other periods?

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:27.850
Well, the instant they found out 
we couldn't pay them this month...

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:31.790
Step right up! The recruiting desk 
for Branch Office #7 is right here!

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:36.090
It's a young, hip, and casual workplace!

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.850
Come work at Branch Office #10!

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.770
No quotas to meet!

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.760
If you have drive and talent, there's no
 limit to how far you can go with us!

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.160
Really? I'm in!

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:48.780
Don't fall for it!

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.990
That's corporate code for,
 "You'll be working 80 hour weeks!"

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:56.520
Nice tip, coming from somebody 
who couldn't even pay me!

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.580
Come on, right this way.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:00.560
Wait!

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.160
The pretty girl doesn't actually work there!

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:06.600
Your co-workers will all be scary men!

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.340
In the end, I was the only one who stayed.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:14.080
These days, good periods can 
get a job anywhere they want.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.640
But any idiot can see what they're doing!

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:20.190
First they draw you in with log in 
bonuses and free gacha rolls,

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:21.690
or maybe they rent a blimp,

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.440
or run web ads saying, "Don't let 
your wife catch you playing this,"

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:28.280
or sponsor tons of soccer 
teams and comedians,

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:32.290
and then when the player base starts to thin,
 say it's "stress-free and relaxing."

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:34.300
My head's spinning.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.620
Choco, is something wrong?

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:39.080
Anyway, I'm just glad you're back.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.790
Liza, Gajeru, and Haru...

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:46.380
Will you rebuild Branch Office #8 with me?

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:50.080
But rebuild how?

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.680
If we've been shut down, we can't
 do our job as periods...

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.780
I've got an idea.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.510
I can't pay much, but...

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:00.640
Please help me.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:02.980
Leave it to me!

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.230
I swore that I'd become a great period here!

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.920
We don't need money!

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:10.450
Right, Gajeru, Liza?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:15.000
Don't worry, Erika-san! Campanella-san!

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.080
The three of us, and Choco and Miu,

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.540
will all work together to 
rebuild the Branch Office!

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:22.660
Haru!

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:28.330
Gajeru, say something!

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:31.090
At this rate, we'll be 
forced to work for free!

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:34.040
Haru, you grew up so fast!

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.970
I'll follow you, too!

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.560
Why are you crying?

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:43.510
Oh, fine. It's not like I've 
got anywhere else to go.

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:45.020
I'll play along for a while.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:48.050
That's just what I'd hoped 
to hear from you three,

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:50.260
Branch Office #8's most useless members!

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.070
Listen, that's not a compliment.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.390
And nobody's ever called me that before.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:57.340
Oh, right, I forgot something important.

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.870
Since we had to sell off everything 
the Branch Office owned,

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:03.080
you're all being evicted.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:03.810
Evicted?

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:05.000
We have to leave our homes?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:05.790
Yup.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:07.710
The movers are probably there right now.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.050
It's all gone!

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:20.680
No! My Sapphire-san collection!

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.770
My completely wasted youth!

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:26.560
Listen, this is my stuff!

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:30.070
I understand that, but somebody's 
already bought it all.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.210
It was all sold for 100 zel apiece.

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:35.320
My stuff isn't that cheap!

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:37.450
I'll buy it all back for 1,000 zel apiece!

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:43.730
Why did I overpay to buy 
back all my own stuff?

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:46.260
You can just buy more clothes, right?

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:48.190
All I've got left of my 
Sapphire-san collection is

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:51.000
this one book I brought with 
me when we went camping!

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.420
But it's awesome!

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.610
Sapphire-san is the best!

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.550
Shut up, you beast!

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:59.410
Didn't you want to go check 
out your room, Haru-kun?

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:01.700
I'm fine as long as Choco is with me.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:03.930
The rest of the stuff wasn't important.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:07.010
Don't say it's not important.

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:08.330
It's rude.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:10.870
It's our home I'm talking about, yeah...

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:13.040
Also, please don't hit me that hard.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:18.070
Erika-san, where are we supposed to live now?

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.990
I'll provide you food, 
clothes, and a place to live.

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:22.540
Use the room next door. It's empty.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:26.130
There's one problem, though...

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:27.500
What's that?

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.250
This place doesn't allow pets!

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.490
No, Miu isn't a pet! He's my Art!　

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.090
I'm afraid that doesn't matter!

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.150
Is Gajeru allowed?

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:41.560
Don't treat me like a pet!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:44.390
Yes.

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:46.970
Miu isn't a pet.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.440
He's very important...

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.030
...as my emergency food supply.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.720
I guess that's okay, then.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.070
I'll let the landlord know.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:11.500
So how are we going to 
rebuild Branch Office #8?

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.420
It's simple.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:17.760
We take quests, defeat spirals,
 and get the rewards.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.090
But HQ shut us down, right?

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:24.530
So we just have to not go through HQ!

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.680
Does that mean...

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:27.680
...we go unlicensed?

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:30.280
We're not so grown-up that we're 
willing to just sit around

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.640
and wait after HQ shuts us down.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.780
If we make enough money to buy 
back our land and buildings,

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.080
and hire periods again,

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:38.950
HQ won't complain.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:44.490
We've already put in a request for quest 
proposals to the nearby villages.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:47.520
"Top secret," "No questions asked,"
"Done in 30 minutes or your quest is free"!

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:52.580
Um, we just need to keep defeating 
spirals like always, right?

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:57.260
Yes. We keep taking any job,
 no matter how crappy,

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.260
and someday, we'll be able to 
rebuild the Branch Office!

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:03.300
Looks like we got a job.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:09.600
It's our first quest!

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:12.300
It's from Stingy Village to the east.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.030
The quest is to... defeat spirals!

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:16.810
Okay.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:19.490
New Branch Office #8, roll out!

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.070
Roger!

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:22.990
You're coming, too, Choco?

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:25.280
Yup. I'll help you all out.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.000
<b>~ the journey to the end of the despair ~</b>

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:36.920
Welcomoney!

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:40.790
I'm Mayor Bigbucks, and I run this place!

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:43.140
Don't look so cents-tense!

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.400
We're not nervous, though.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:47.420
He looks like an arrogant jackass.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:48.720
Well, he is a mayor.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.850
Cramming money jokes into a guy's
 dialogue is lazy writing.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:55.060
I'll lead you right to the spiral payday!

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.700
Follow me, money!

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:57.820
Okay...

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:01.950
The spirals only recently
 cashed in on our area.

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:05.530
They're bothering the villagers,
 so we cashed you in!

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:09.620
Is there a reason you asked 
us instead of Arc End?

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:13.360
'Cause I don't have to
 pay you guys the big bucks!

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:16.590
You guys are working for half-off MSRP!

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.630
H-Half?!

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:20.560
He's right...

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.660
Why so cheap?

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:25.050
I think Campanella said something about it.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:30.180
Listen, the key in business 
is to make it up on volume!

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:30.180
That.

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.550
You're kidding me!

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:34.520
We're the ones doing the work, not her!

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.550
Shut your money makers!

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:39.300
Look, there's your spiral payday!

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:42.110
Spirals...

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.030
Most of them are Level 1, but look.

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:47.500
Level 2?

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.170
That wasn't in the quest text!

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.540
He's got the nastiest price tag of 'em all!

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.480
Make sure you cash his check!

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:54.620
Got it.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:57.660
All right, get out there and get paid!

00:12:58.560 --> 00:12:59.540
Wait.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.880
We're supposed to get paid up front.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.740
Who cares?

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:08.100
I'll pay your invoice when the work's done,
 so what difference does it make?

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.680
Listen, we're taking the risks here.

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.790
You need to abide by the contract.

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.010
I know your game, gold digger.

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:17.710
You just want to take the money and run!

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:19.630
We're periods!

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:22.280
When we take a job, we do it!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.160
Fine, but I'm the skinflint
 mayor of Stingy Village!

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:28.200
I promise to pay you when you're done,money!

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.470
Then pay up front.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:32.190
We're already working for dirt cheap.

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:33.850
Then I can pay you later!

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:35.050
Since you're working for dirt cheap, money!

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:36.840
Pay us up front, okay?

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:39.230
Or we won't get rid of your spirals!

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:41.040
Money...

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:43.800
You guys take plastic?

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.420
We're cash only!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.730
Hold it right there!

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:51.010
There's no need to pay those periods a thing!

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:57.600
Wh-Who are you?

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.400
Mizaru!

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:07.740
Kikazaru!

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.080
Iwazaru and Guru!

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.660
Together we are...

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:14.100
WI!

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:14.370
SE!

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:14.690
MA!

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:15.160
N!

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.980
Wiseman!

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.090
Wiseman?

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.140
That's right, guru!

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:27.670
We're heroes whose job it is to 
teach you periods a lesson, guru!

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:29.060
What?

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:31.640
Another lazily-written character has arrived.

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:33.890
Hey, Mr. Mayor!

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:38.500
We'll get rid of your spiral problem 
for you cheaper than the periods will!

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.530
Why not hire us instead?

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:42.310
Really cheap?

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.940
We never lie, guru.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.630
And we take credit cards, too,

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:48.450
and offer points in a variety 
of rewards programs!

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:51.190
Cheapness is money justice!

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:53.410
Okay, you Wiseman guys get the payday!

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.870
Hey! That wasn't the deal!

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:58.320
We were the ones you hired!

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:03.350
And he's firing you, and hiring us again!

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:05.690
Hell no! That quest is ours!

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:06.880
It's ours!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.210
Now, now, money.

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:12.480
If you both want the quest that badly,

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:15.080
have a one-on-one duel in the village square,

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.310
and the winner gets the payday!

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.730
D-Duel?

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:20.650
Step right up!

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.940
Admission fee is just 5 zel!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:28.150
Special and platinum seating for
 high rollers is almost sold out!

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:30.590
That mayor is amazing.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:33.380
He's making more off this than 
he's paying for the quest.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.120
Yeah, we could learn a lesson from him.

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:37.800
Listen, do I really have to do this?

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:38.690
Of course.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:40.940
You want to rebuild the Branch Office, right?

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.000
Yeah.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.370
I've gotta do my best!

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.170
Okay, who's fighting from your side?

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:52.590
I'm afraid it won't be me, 
Kikazaru, or Iwazaru, either!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:54.760
That's your cue!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:05.610
That's...

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:12.060
The Legendary Beastman, Nero-san!

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:12.800
And that's his...

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:14.990
...ultra-rare five-star version!

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.120
It's all humans.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.540
Disgusting.

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:23.080
Scared?

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.340
He's our bodyguard for the day.

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:28.040
I'm glad we had him come along, guru.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.760
Teach 'em a lesson, guru.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:33.340
They summoned me, so I won't refuse.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.850
W-Wait a second!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.440
I-I can't!

00:16:42.440 --> 00:16:45.260
I can't fight that guy! Not alone!

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:47.660
Even all of us together couldn't beat him!

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.770
Nobody said they'd be summoning a five-star!

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:52.420
He said he was "summoned"...

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.360
But how did they summon him, and from where?

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:57.080
Forget that. What do we do about this duel?

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:59.590
Time to take one for the team, Haru!

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:00.730
No!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.710
You in trouble?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.630
The Wandering Call Girl, Iona-chan, is here!

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:11.880
Iona?

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:14.710
"Call girl" doesn't mean
 what she thinks it does...

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:17.920
Who are you? What's that carriage?

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:22.310
Oh, you don't know about calls?

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:26.720
Calls are how you summon new party members!

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:29.010
You put the luna stones in here,

00:17:29.010 --> 00:17:31.540
and the new party member comes out here!

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.190
Really simple, right?

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:34.300
Y-Yeah!

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:40.630
Wait, if make a Call, we can get a 
strong party member to beat that guy?

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:42.880
Yeah, it's possible.

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:44.560
Haru, make a Call!

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:45.670
Me?

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:48.900
We can make a "Call" if we get 
enough luna stones, right?

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:49.860
How much are they?

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:52.920
We can pay up to 3,315 zel!

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.540
How did you know how much 
money I had in my wallet?

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:58.580
I'm sorry, but you can't 
buy luna stones with zel.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:17:59.470
Only yen!

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.790
Clang, clang, clang!

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:02.810
Yen?

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:03.740
What is a "yen"?

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:06.760
But you guys are new customers...

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.150
Okay, I've got it!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:11.290
I'll give you one free Call today!

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:12.320
R-Really?

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.190
Yup!

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:14.530
Iona-chan never lies!

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.900
Whew! Maybe we can win now!

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.110
Great news, huh, Haru?

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.530
Yeah, now I don't have to die!

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:21.740
Okay, time for the Call!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:32.920
Boom!

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:43.510
A strong comrade... is coming!

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:52.900
Come and get me!

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.800
Wh-Why...?

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:58.600
Why did we get a one-star?

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:01.040
That's weaker than we are!

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:04.740
And he's a fire-type,
 while that guy's a water-type!

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:08.450
Calls have set probabilities, 
so sometimes that happens.

00:19:08.970 --> 00:19:10.750
Call again sometime!

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.460
Bye-bye!

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:16.240
Hey, let's do this.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.660
The cash prize winner is Wiseman!

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:28.470
Now the quest is ours!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.880
Thanks for your help, guru.

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:34.650
I was hoping for a stronger opponent.

00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:38.010
See you around!

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:41.150
That's a message from our employer, guru.

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:44.320
What?

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:46.910
The mission is canceled. Retreat?

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:54.430
Well, I didn't expect Wiseman
 to ditch me and my money.

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:59.510
But to tell you the truth, I wanted to pay
 you guys to do that job from the start!

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:02.200
I'm afraid we lost,

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.320
and probably can't help you.

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:06.860
Don't say that, money!

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:09.150
Please, money!

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:10.980
Can you believe this guy?

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:11.920
Huh, Haru?

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.040
Yeah...

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:14.270
But...

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:18.230
The villagers won't be safe until 
the spirals are defeated, right?

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.960
You'll do it, money?

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:21.560
Yes.

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:23.240
That's why we came!

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.620
That's such a huge bonus!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.530
You're such a softie.

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:29.490
Oh, well.

00:20:29.800 --> 00:20:31.160
That's just who Haru is.

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:40.710
Ice Edge!

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:47.390
Full-power attack!

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:54.630
Is this... an Art?

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:58.230
Hey, what's the deal?

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:00.550
We defeated the periods,

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:03.440
so why'd you tell us to just come home?

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:04.570
Yeah! Yeah!

00:21:04.920 --> 00:21:06.840
It's okay, isn't it?

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:09.910
You managed to beat up the periods.

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:13.350
We'll just call this our way 
of introducing ourselves.

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:13.870
Okay?

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.050
Got it.

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:19.720
You're paying us a fortune.

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:20.500
We'll do what you say.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.260
Thanks!

00:21:24.440 --> 00:21:25.680
Oh, Luluna-chan.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.360
Are you awake?

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.680
Yeah. Good morning.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.260
It's almost night, though.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.850
Good work, Haru-kun!

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.310
It sounds like it was rough,

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:38.210
but your first mission was a success.

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:39.460
Well done!

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:40.820
Thank you!

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:43.540
That was exhausting.

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:47.020
There's no way in hell that 
was worth the money we got.

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:50.520
Don't say that. This is a period's job.

00:21:50.520 --> 00:21:53.550
But who's that guy?

00:21:53.550 --> 00:21:56.080
Oh, um, he just kind of followed us.

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:04.960
<i>The road to rebuilding Branch Office 
#8 is going to be a long one.</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Episode 2
"Hot Springs Custom"</b>

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:38.150
"Hot Springs Custom."
